    <!-- Security card -->
    <string name="security_title">🔒 Security &amp; Coach Setup</string>
    <string name="security_instructions"><![CDATA[
<b>Creating a safe GitHub token:</b><br/><br/>
1. GitHub → Profile → <b>Settings</b> → <b>Developer settings</b>.<br/>
2. <b>Personal access tokens → Fine-grained tokens → Generate new token</b>.<br/>
3. <b>Token name:</b> FLL Tablet - Robot Game Sync<br/>
4. <b>Expiration:</b> End of season (e.g. 90 days).<br/>
5. <b>Repository access:</b> Only select repositories → pick your team repo.<br/>
6. <b>Permissions → Repository permissions:</b><br/>
   • <b>Contents: Read and write</b> (allows pushing code/files).<br/>
   • <b>Issues: Read and write</b> (allows Sticky Note Kanban board sync).<br/>
   • <b>Metadata: Read-only</b> (auto-set, required).<br/>
   • Everything else: <b>No access</b>.<br/>
7. <b>Account permissions:</b> All <b>No access</b>.<br/><br/>

<b>Why this is safe:</b><br/>
• The token can only see ONE repo — your other repos are invisible.<br/>
• No Administration permission — cannot delete/rename the repo.<br/>
• GitHub blocks deleting the main branch — even without paid rulesets.<br/>
• This app only uses forward commits — history can never be erased.<br/>
• Token is encrypted on the tablet (Android Keystore).<br/>
• Coach tip: run <tt>git pull</tt> on your laptop occasionally as a backup.
    ]]></string>

